# Database migrations

The schema change on a branch is an edit to `packages/api/migrations/current.sql`. Commit that file with the rest of the work.

Do not run `npm run db:commit` or `graphile-migrate commit`. Do not create, edit, or stage files under `packages/api/migrations/committed/`. Those commands write the next numbered migration. Parallel branches each take that same number and conflict.

Run `npm run db:commit` or `graphile-migrate commit` only when the user explicitly tells you to, in this conversation, immediately before merging to master.

`npm run db:watch` and `npm run db:migrate` are fine. `db:migrate` applies numbered migrations that already exist. Do not edit `packages/api/schema.sql`. It is generated.
